        "editorial_notes": "Original project-authored definition, example, and image brief. Retail module03 editorial decision: Retain the broad purchased-goods carrier, including reusable bags; the accepted illustration does not specify material or require visible contents. Retain shopping bag. Carrier bag is not added globally because the consulted British alternative corresponds specifically to the paper/plastic sense, narrower than the selected broad purchased-goods-carrier sense. Independent AI editorial language review was completed on 2026-10-16 for the selected noun sense, part of speech, definition, original example, and evidenced accepted forms; no human or subject-matter credential is claimed. Domain review is not required for the current memberships. Independent AI morphology review was completed on 2026-10-16 for this exact graph at the documented modern-stem depth; this is not human or subject-matter approval. The shopping-bag image has completed scoped carrier picture review. The accepted plain open bag brief replaces the original fabric, flexible-side and visible-purchases requirements, which are not depicted. Empty gift bags may share this form; intended shopping use is supplied by context. The original brief and its mismatch remain in retained provenance. The exact Ava word recording has user listening approval and is integrated. CEFR difficulty remains a provisional editorial estimate. This record alone does not make any course or module ready."
